  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a severe downward bias when the recent price trend is upward or volatile; true outcomes consistently spike significantly higher than predicted (e.g., +5% to +10% deviation) during periods of high volatility.",
    "The model fails to capture immediate momentum shifts, resulting in a lag where it predicts a continuation of the previous day's lower level while the true outcome reacts strongly to the most recent price action.",
    "Sentiment history shows no predictive power for short-term spikes; corrections should ignore sentiment signals and instead weight the last 3-5 days of actual price data more heavily than the model's trend assumption.",
    "Apply an upward correction factor (approx. +4% to +6%) to the forecasted value when the historical volatility over the last 18 days exceeds 20% or when the most recent true outcome deviates >3% from the immediate prior.",
    "The model systematically underestimates the amplitude of mean-reversion events, predicting a smoother path while true outcomes show sharp peaks followed by rapid declines within the same 30-day horizon."
  ]
}
